n than the serverless VPC  access connector  for this you must use a different  network and assign it an IP range of  10.8.0.0  28 to the connector this ensures that  the source IP address for any request  sent from the connector will be from  this IP range  before we get started ensure the  following prerequisites are met the  organization policy name resource  location constraint allows you to deploy  the Google Cloud functions in the  specific region and the apis listed here  are enabled to understand how this works  let's dive into a demo as a prerequisite  you will need to have a postgres  instance created with a database defined  and some sample data refer to the quick  start link provided in the description  to learn how to do this  here we already have created an instance  name my postgres which contains a  database name guestbook with a table  named entries  next go to Cloud functions page here we  have deployed a cloud functions named  connect postgres that connects to a  postgres DP instance name my postgres  and runs a search query  please note we will be using this Cloud  functions in all the three scenarios in  our demo  in the first scenario the cloud SQL  instance is accessible over public IP  and is in the same region U.S Central 1  as Cloud functions  that's the function yay it is successful  now let's move the cloud SQL instance to  a VPC network with a private IP and  allocate an IP range for this  edit the instance select private IP  under the connection section  choose the network of your preference in  this example we will use the default  Network  allocate an IP range  and create a connection  test the same Cloud functions oops it's  failing with an exception  check the logs to see if you have any  further details we see  Cloud SQL connection field error  why does this error occur  this error occurs because we do not have  a serverless VPC access connector in the  same network as the cloud SQL instance  to address this issue go to VPC Network  and select serverless VPC access  create a serverless VPC access connector  in the default network with IP range  10.8.0.0 28  let's name it test connector  ensure the connector is in the same  region as the cloud functions U.S  Central One in our case  Let's test the function again  it's successful and we are getting the  output of the select query as expected  finally let's try to connect the cloud  SQL instance hosted in a different  region than the connector  create a cloud SQL instance in Us East  one while our existing connector is in  US Central One  we have created a cloud SQL instance  name my postgres2  ensure the cloud function and SQL  instance are using the same network  let's quickly update the functions  variable with the new instance details  and test it wow congratulations it is  successful  for more information on connecting  directly to resources on your virtual  private Cloud network from serverless  environments check out this  documentation thanks for watching  foreign  [Music]

